  "ingredients": [
    "1/2 medium lemon",
    "2 tablespoon avocado oil",
    "1 tablespoon water",
    "1/2 teaspoon vanilla extract",
    "1 cup almond flour",
    "3 tablespoon stevia/erythritol blend",
    "salt (pinch of )",
    "4 tablespoon powdered stevia/erythritol blend",
    "2 teaspoon lemon juice (as needed)"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Measure out and prepare all the ingredients. Preheat oven to 350F.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-lemon-donut-holes/#wprm-recipe-53553-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2020/10/Lemon-Donut-Holes-1.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Line a baking sheet with parchment paper.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-lemon-donut-holes/#wprm-recipe-53553-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2020/10/Lemon-Donut-Holes-2.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cut the lemon into small wedges and remove the seeds.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-lemon-donut-holes/#wprm-recipe-53553-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2020/10/Lemon-Donut-Holes-3.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Place the lemon wedges, avocado oil, water, and vanilla extract into a blender. Blend on medium until smooth, then remove any small pieces that will not blend.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-lemon-donut-holes/#wprm-recipe-53553-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2020/10/Lemon-Donut-Holes-4.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the almond flour, stevia/erythritol blend, and salt. Continue to blend until thickened and dough forms.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-lemon-donut-holes/#wprm-recipe-53553-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2020/10/Lemon-Donut-Holes-5.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "With a cookie scooper or dinner spoon, form balls and roll until smooth with your hands. Place these on the parchment-lined baking sheet. Bake in the oven for 10-12 minutes.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-lemon-donut-holes/#wprm-recipe-53553-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2020/10/Lemon-Donut-Holes-6.png"
    },
    {
      "text": "In a bowl, make the glaze by adding powdered stevia/erythritol blend and lemon juice. Add the lemon juice a little bit at a time, stirring together until a smooth glaze forms. Optionally, add yellow food coloring to the glaze.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-lemon-donut-holes/#wprm-recipe-53553-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2020/10/Lemon-Donut-Holes-7.png"
    },
    {
      "text": "Once the donuts come out of the oven, let them cool.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-lemon-donut-holes/#wprm-recipe-53553-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2020/10/Lemon-Donut-Holes-8.png"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dip the donut holes into the lemon glaze. You may serve right away!",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/keto-lemon-donut-holes/#wprm-recipe-53553-step-0-8",
      "imageSource": null
    }
  ],
